  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Right now it's difficult to deal with playerapi functions because in the editor, anything you do with them results in null reference and halts the script. you have to check for null and then do a completely different set of actions if you want your scripts to still function. It would be very convenient if there was a packaged up player emulator where you could pull information like a displayname, tracking data, bone positions, etc.",
